A template wrapper can expose a slot for its text and one for inline styles.
A style helper supplies a named insert to the same element.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    heading #= [$html:<h2 style="[$slot style]">[$slot]</h2>]
    strong #= [$html:<strong>[$slot]</strong>]
    heavy #= [$in style:font-weight: 700;]
    red #= [$in style:color: red;]

    [heading, heavy, red:Build status]
    [heading, red:Build status: [strong:experimental]]
]

The first heading receives both CSS declarations in source order. The second
contains a strong element around just the word `experimental`. Nest a
second element explicitly. Style helpers can share their receiver's head.

### Carry a stylesheet with a component

A shared support package can return markup and a tracked stylesheet as an
ordinary struct. This example defines its own component API.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    -- components/@package.moth
    $export
    HtmlPart = | body String, stylesheet String |

    $export
    docs_sidebar #|heading String| -> HtmlPart {
        return HtmlPart(
            body = [$html:<aside class="docs-sidebar"><h2>[heading]</h2></aside>],
            stylesheet = @sidebar.css
        )
    }
]

An entry imports the component and contributes its stylesheet and body
separately. The HTML builder resolves the CSS URL for this page.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    -- docs/@entry.moth
    @components docs_sidebar
    @introduction content as introduction

    sidebar #= docs_sidebar("Documentation")
    [$in title:Functions]
    [$in stylesheets:[sidebar.stylesheet]]
    [sidebar.body]
    [introduction]
]

Each direct `stylesheets` insert supplies one tracked CSS resource. The
builder keeps the first contribution for a repeated resource.

### Use a named template slot

A smaller helper can stay a template rather than become a new type:

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    card #= [$html:
        <article class="card">
            <h2>[$slot title]</h2>
            [$slot]
        </article>
    ]

    [card:
        [$in title:Functions]
        Body content
    ]
]

The `title` insert fills the card's own named slot. It never searches ancestor
templates or sends a builder message. Body content lands in the default slot.

Keep using slots while a helper needs no typed result and no resource
dependency. Reach for a component value when the page needs both.

See @../../templates (Templates) for other slot and wrapper forms.
